title: '[EPMB] Let DAP own and authorise payouts from its buffer'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    DAP now owns every outflow from its buffer, mirroring the deactivation it already does on
    inflow. It gains a registry of capped draws (`BufferDraws`), each with an absolute budget per
    drip period rather than a `Perbill` share of issuance, set by `BudgetOrigin` through the new
    `set_draw_budget` call. `pallet_dap::BufferDraw<T, Key>` hands a registered draw to any pallet
    that needs paying out of the buffer, so the consumer requests a payment instead of holding the
    buffer account and transferring from it. DAP authorises against the budget, moves the funds and
    reactivates them.

    `signed::Config::RewardSource` is now `sp_staking::budget::PaymentSource`, a single atomic
    `pay` instead of the previous `account()` plus `paid()` pair. `ReactivatingPot` is removed:
    reactivation belongs to DAP, not to the paying pallet. `ActivePot` stays for pots holding
    active funds and gains a `Currency` type parameter to cover the minting (`None`) case.

    Asset Hub Westend and the staking-async parachain runtime swap
    `ReactivatingPot<SignedRewardPot, Balances>` for
    `pallet_dap::BufferDraw<Runtime, signed::RewardBudgetKey>`, and register the draw at genesis
    through the new DAP genesis config, or on existing chains through
    `pallet_dap::migrations::MigrateV2ToV3`.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    Signed-phase election rewards are still paid out of the DAP buffer, but now through DAP itself
    and capped by a per-drip-period budget. A payout over that budget is refused and the reward is
    queued in `UnpaidRewards`, claimable later via `claim_unpaid_reward` exactly as when the buffer
    is short of funds.
crates:
- name: pallet-dap
  bump: major
- name: sp-staking
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-election-provider-multi-block
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: pallet-staking-async-parachain-runtime
  bump: minor
